{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T11:59:38.617522Z","id":"209688db9e5a88f20bff13f2808aec416c6cde524fb9525d8ca5ec16ef3368dc","body":{"detail":"ChangeTracker starts longpress-landed only in sent() (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart:76-86), which runs on the shell's 'sent' host message after its own composer's Send; workerWorking() adds the change untimed. A thread created with POST /api/artifacts/<id>/threads and sent with POST .../threads/<tid>/send reaches the worker and lands (checked on macOS with a real daemon, WebView and FileTimings at e51b5922: version 2 published, thread resolved with the agent reply), but no shell 'sent' is posted, so timings.jsonl holds only say-usable. The step's last assertion ('one long-press→landed record') needs the shell's Send itself, for example by driving the shell's composer through WebViewAppSurface.evaluate, or the assertion has to move to a test that posts the shell's 'sent' message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1131},"content_hash":"13906562209d5cd49e0c49daac85d2ce4bbd5d994a9c1ab64576c8db280ced4b"},"summary":"A thread sent over the API never starts the long-press to landed timing, so this step's expected record cannot appear","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-18-professional-ui.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:42:02.009027Z","id":"423bce14e1032e1df327057b97722b286ff8f0d1ee3fafb002ac5fb1840f196d","body":{"detail":"Failure: any app install. Store::set_session_name (crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs:921-944) lowercases the name and refuses one in clax_core::names::RESERVED (crates/clax-core/src/names.rs:13: agent, owner, clax, me, everyone) with 400 invalid_name, before the name_taken and name_locked checks Decision 10 plans to tolerate. So the worker's renameSession(_sid, 'Clax') would fail on every registration, and the session keeps its derived name (app, app-2). Even when allowed, names are stored lowercase, so the session would read \"clax\", not \"Clax\". The worker rename was not implemented. What the person sees already reads Clax without it: since 8db49096c the shell names harness app \"Clax\" whatever the session's name (web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts harnessName and agentNames, web/shell/src/q/model.ts agentLabel, web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte), and the Flutter thread page names agent comments \"Clax\" (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart _comment). The derived name still shows where the shell prints a session's raw name: the browser shell's People, Roster, Inbox filter and comment author labels (sidebar-model authorLabel uses a.name).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":552},"end":{"line":566},"content_hash":"deb00213b825f68644f168357c7a23a9dd24506c38836d805e64d8a4de3d88b9"},"suggested_fix":"Choose one: (a) drop the rename and keep the harness-based label as the one rule (no daemon change); (b) let the app harness take the reserved name (a Rust change in set_session_name, against Decision 10's no-Rust-changes), and decide whether the stored lowercase \"clax\" is acceptable; (c) give sessions a display name separate from the @-mention name.","summary":"Task 16's rename of the app's session to \"Clax\" can never succeed: \"clax\" is a reserved agent name, so PATCH /api/sessions/{id} answers 400 invalid_name","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:7.2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:00:57.101583Z","id":"b8d63c9686a534abec710178ce4ffce4a740458219c588e49e0c99f6986f74e4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs:9 ALPHABET is lowercase Crockford base32 without i, l, o, u, so ArtifactId::parse refuses abcdefghijkl and the core's admit (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs content_host) refuses a content frame for it. apps/clax_app/test/core/frame_test.dart asserts idOfHost('abcdefghijkl.c.clax.invalid') is null and uses abcdefghjkmn instead. Task 14's spike (lines 930 and 936) frames the content origin of abcdefghijkl and would be refused by the core for the same reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":854},"end":{"line":854},"content_hash":"a58a0b4f67669ac1337a2bf7cc415d189b6dd4a3a325f09d3228856bb451ff95"},"summary":"The plan's example artifact ID abcdefghijkl is not one: i and l are outside the ID alphabet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:31.702434Z","id":"f705e2a53c14aec7938e241ad6a4cc254140c1380264ef905158ce83b4f91ad0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:df84e854c","summary":"Fixed in df84e854c: Task 12 Step 1 and Task 14 (expectIsolated and Step 1's spike page) now use abcdefghjkmn. grep -n abcdefghijkl on the plan finds it only in Task 12's example of a host idOfHost refuses, and in Task 10's origin.test.ts template substitution (line 734), which never parses an ID.","supersedes":"b8d63c9686a534abec710178ce4ffce4a740458219c588e49e0c99f6986f74e4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:36:38.617508Z","id":"b4192efc80d157c69043b966a3872245b9930db0f1dec26f0c03c9d046f7bc95","body":{"detail":"Event::Job (crates/clax-core/src/events.rs:203) carries {id, client, state, step, rev}, no row, so there is no JobChanged(Job): the event is JobNoticed, and a rev above the held one emits ReadJob(jobId) (GET /api/jobs/{id}), answered by JobRead(effect, jobId, Job?) (null when the core holds no row). Event::JobsOwner is OwnerChanged({client, held}) and replaces OwnerReleased; a claim answered 409 owner_draining is OwnerDraining. Job.questions is Map<String, JobAnswer> (pending, answered, declined, withdrawn, as clax_store::jobs::JobAnswer), not String?. Ask and Publish carry the turn and the call ID; Committed carries questionId for an Ask. Added: Refusal Invalid(code, message) for any other 4xx; StopWork(jobId) (the runner abandons a job's work: cancelJob); OutOfTime (running jobs pause, spec 7.6); Change carries the artifact's base version. ClaimOwner, LoadJobs and ProbeClaude are not recorded in inFlight; toJson/fromJson is left to Task 25's codec.dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1367},"end":{"line":1391},"content_hash":"3088354bd7cb5e43475bfdf0a5dbfe63bd6ee52c7162bff133a6b45e42ee5915"},"summary":"Task 24's Msg and Effect lists differ from the queue as built (apps/clax_app/lib/queue/msg.dart, effect.dart), where the store's model differs; Task 25's runner and codec follow the code","tags":["plan","queue","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:09:09.397919Z","id":"b648ec8170217499bb82b4521e96163aa171b120abb648849f943980b40b8f15","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/content_hash.dart contentHash hashes one line '<path>\\0<sha256 hex of the bytes>\\0<size>\\n' per file and prefixes 'sha256:', and spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §8.2 says the digest is that content hash. crates/clax-core/src/digest.rs follows content_hash.dart and the spec (its vector is checked by apps/clax_app/test/bundle/files_digest_test.dart); the plan's interface text is the outlier.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1305},"end":{"line":1308},"content_hash":"d68c59afc5084285b016a1f82e5a6c584137f90f4b755dd6078906971b565b83"},"suggested_fix":"Change the plan's doc comment to content_hash.dart's line form.","summary":"Task 23's files_digest doc describes lines '<path>\\0<len>\\0<bytes>', which is not what content_hash.dart computes","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
